rompt.md","size_bytes":181},"prompt_steps":{"digest":"f76989cdc187e90787a9ab36963f46515f2f138d9d5ff16dea680c70bd8384aa","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-ij.1/prompt_steps.json","size_bytes":14318},"state":{"digest":"3ed86f2f6a41d59909f89861402c2367657a5ef77dba13a4306346a4af4918c0","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-ij.1/state.json","size_bytes":183}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-ij.1","local_name":"sase-ij.1","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-ij","agent_clan_generation":"20260809152310","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-ij.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-ij[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Ratchet the sase-core-rs window at the release boundary instead of [/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]         [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]on feature PRs[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]A feature agent can call a newly landed sase-core binding or [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]behavior without editing pyproject.toml, uv.lock, or a version [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]literal, and without waiting on a core release; the published-floor[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]invariant is enforced once, mechanically, on the pending sase [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]release instead of ~1.2 times a day by a dedicated agent.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]8[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]core_window_ratchet.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/core_window_ratchet.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-ij[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-ij/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Derive the telemetry smoke test's expected minimum from [/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]pyproject[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]derive-floor-literal[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]derive-floor-literal: replace the hardcoded \"0.21.3\" golden assertion in[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tests/test_sase_core_rs_telemetry_smoke_tool.py with a value derived [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]from pyproject.toml, so a floor change stops requiring a test edit.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Build the window ratchet tool[/bold #D7AFFF]                                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]ratchet-tool[dim] · [dim][/dim]after derive-floor-literal[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ratchet-tool: add a stdlib-only tools/ratchet_core_window that selects [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the newest fully published stable sase-core-rs from PyPI, rewrites only [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]that requirement in pyproject.toml through one tested ceiling-policy [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]function, refreshes uv.lock with a bounded diff guard, and supports [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]--check/--report-only with idempotence and downgrade refusal.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Enforce the published floor on the release branch and at [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]publish time[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]release-lane[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]release-lane: add a CI job that runs only on the release-please branch [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and validates the exact declared PyPI core floor against bindings, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]wire-schema probes, smokes and the contract set, and pin the floor [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]exactly in publish.yml's install-smoke so an incompatible floor [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]mechanically blocks the PyPI upload.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Ratchet the window on the pending release branch in [/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]report-only mode[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]release-ratchet[dim] · [dim][/dim]after ratchet-tool[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]release-ratchet: extend publish.yml's sync-lockfile job into a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sync-release-metadata reconciler that runs the ratchet tool ahead of the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]lock refresh, landing it in report-only mode so a real release can be [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]observed before it writes anything.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Verify one report-only run and switch the ratchet to apply[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]enable-ratchet[dim] · [dim][/dim]after release-lane, release-ratchet[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]enable-ratchet: read the report-only output from at least one real [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]master push with a pending release branch, confirm the proposed version [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and diff are exactly right, then flip the reconciler to apply and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]confirm the release branch stays green.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Stop conscripting feature agents into the floor bump[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]retire-conscription[dim] · [dim][/dim]after enable-ratchet[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]retire-conscription: remove published-core-minimum-smoke from feature [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]PRs and master pushes now that the invariant is enforced at the release [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]boundary, and rewrite the three Justfile warnings and the docs that [/#D7D7AF]\n 